# --- Live Tail -------------------------------------------------------------
# Streams matching logs to the browser over SSE, matched on the ingest pod before the
# TimeFusion/Postgres write. No configuration: it is on, and it works with or without Kafka.
#
# Transport is derived from KAFKA_BROKERS, which you already set:
#   brokers configured  -> the `live_tail` Kafka topic (create it with short retention:
#                          rpk topic create live_tail -p 6 -r 1 \
#                            -c retention.ms=600000 -c retention.bytes=67108864)
#   no brokers          -> the projects.live_tail_events relay table, so a deployment
#                          without Kafka still gets a working tail and needs no new
#                          infrastructure.
#
# Everything else (lease length, queue depths, per-user and per-project caps) is a constant
# in Pkg.LiveTail — none of it is a deployment decision.
